    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0331" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115A P.W./2–145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Huddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-01T08:00:00+01:00">February 1, 1945—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:39 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>704. American Interests—Japan. Legation’s 7433, November 9th.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d195-f1"/> Foreign Office note January 25th states Swiss Legation,
                    Tokyo reports it again approached Japanese Foreign Office to obtain information
                    regarding murder 17 Americans in Philippines mentioned in Department’s 3532,
                    October 16th.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d195-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d195-f1" n="9" xml:id="d195-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; but for summary, see <ref target="frus1944v05#pg_1006">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1944, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>, p. 1006</ref>, footnote 81.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d195-f2" n="10" xml:id="d195-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1944v05#pg_1006">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>, p. 1006</ref>. In airgram A–411, March
                    12, 10 a.m. (740.00115A PW/3–1245), the Minister in Switzerland reported that
                    the Swiss Legation at Tokyo had made renewed representations on March 3 to the
                    Japanese Foreign Office with a view to obtaining the information requested in
                    telegram 3532.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
